# Version Management

## Who chooses the version

| Entry point | Who picks the number |
|-------------|----------------------|
| `/twincat3-cmd-release` / skill `twincat3-release` | **User** — ask for exact `MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD.REVISION`; do not auto-bump |
| `/twincat3-cmd-new-version` / skill `twincat3-new-version` | **Rule-based auto** — classify changes, apply bump table below; ask only if ambiguous; honor explicit user override |

Agents must **not** invent a version outside this table. Show current via
`twincat_plcproj_info` when helpful.

## Version Format

`MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD.REVISION` — e.g. `0.0.0.1`, `1.0.0.0`, `1.2.3.45`

### Bump table (for humans and for `/twincat3-cmd-new-version`)

| Change scope (since last released version / relevant commits) | Increment | Resets |
|---------------------------------------------------------------|-----------|--------|
| Breaking / incompatible API | **MAJOR** +1 | MINOR, BUILD, REVISION → 0 |
| New feature, backwards-compatible | **MINOR** +1 | BUILD, REVISION → 0 |
| Bug fix | **BUILD** +1 | REVISION → 0 |
| Internal / patch only | **REVISION** +1 | — |

Prefer the **dominant** user-facing change when classifying. Mixed / unclear → ask once.

## Where versions live

| Location | What |
|----------|------|
| `.plcproj` `<ProjectVersion>` | Engineering project version |
| `GVLs/Global_Version.TcGVL` | `stLibVersion : ST_LibVersion` (`Tc2_System`) |
| `Versions/<ver>/` | `.library` + `.compiled-library` + `changelog-<ver>.md` |

Both `.plcproj` and `stLibVersion` **must match**. XML/ST samples and folder
tree → `rules/examples/twincat3-versioning.md`.

On **release** / **new-version**, always ship both `.library` and
`.compiled-library` (skills `twincat3-release` / `twincat3-new-version`). The
online-test shortcut (`.library` only) is not a release.

## CI-managed files (do not edit on release)

Do **not** manually update:

- `README.md` download table (AUTO-GENERATED markers)
- `Versions/release_dates.txt`

Repos with the corresponding GitHub Actions workflow refresh these after push. Bot commits that touch them are expected — do not recreate that work by hand.

## Changelog Format

For detailed changelog writing, use the `twincat3-changelog` skill.
For thematic local commits (never push), use the `twincat3-git-commit` skill.

Key rules:
- English only; user-facing impact only (no implementation noise)
- One file per version in `Versions/X.X.X.X/changelog-X.X.X.X.md`
- **Slim-first:** `# Changelog — <LibName> X.X.X.X` with Highlights (≤5) → Added/Changed/Fixed as needed → Migration only if action required
- Full detail only for breaking/major API changes; omit Style sections
- Link each Highlight to the GitHub commit: `https://github.com/<Org>/<Repo>/commit/<sha>` from `git remote get-url origin`
- Breaking changes use `> [!CAUTION]` with **BREAKING CHANGE:**
- Code examples (`iecst`) only when users must wire a new API
